# GitHub's language statistics count bytes of tracked files, so a single generated
# report outweighs the whole source tree: one 790 KB leaderboard.html against 722 KB
# of Python across 68 files, reported as an HTML project. The published report is
# output, not source -- it is produced by src/safety_eval/reporting/ from a run's
# results.json and is committed so a reader can see a real report without running the
# pipeline. Marking it generated excludes it from the language bar and collapses it in
# diffs, where a regenerated 790 KB file is noise.
#
# The Jinja template it is rendered from IS source and is deliberately not marked.
results/published/*.html linguist-generated=true
